abstract: >-
  Object detection and instance segmentation of individual chickens in dense,
  high-occlusion overhead poultry imagery, together with a domain-aware
  synthetic copy-paste augmentation pipeline for dense instance segmentation.

  This is an engineering contribution rather than a new technique: it builds on
  established context-aware copy-paste augmentation (Ghiasi et al., CVPR 2021)
  and Reinhard-style statistical colour transfer (Reinhard et al., 2001), with a
  domain-specific parameterization for flock imagery. Curated, unoccluded
  instance cutouts are composited into training scenes on the fly. A pasted
  instance's size is drawn from a Normal distribution fitted to the target
  scene's own instance-size distribution — an alternative to the depth- or
  perspective-derived scaling used elsewhere in the literature — motivated by
  how a real cohort's weight, and therefore apparent size, spreads out as it
  ages. Colour and size statistics are pooled spatially locally, from real
  instances within a radius of the paste location, in LAB space; placement is
  rejection-sampled against an occupancy map so pastes do not bury existing
  instances.

  The pipeline is dataset-agnostic and framework-independent at its core; the
  implementation here is demonstrated on the ChickenVerse dataset and integrated
  into an Ultralytics YOLO26 training loop. The repository also documents the
  implementation findings in full, including negative results and several
  silent-corruption bugs found along the way.
